# oracle: fix deform/pressure x trate 0.1 y volume z volume vol/balance/p yes (the docs example, with max/rate 0.2) on a 4 x 3 x 3 fcc LJ liquid: the y and z strain rates that keep pyy = pzz at constant volume; compute temp/deform reads the box rates
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# Measured with native LAMMPS: engine vs native thermo 7.6e-10, atoms 8.0e-10 in 160 steps. Without max/rate the rates divide by differences of consecutive pressures and the 2e-15 rounding difference of the step-0 pressure grows about tenfold every few steps (1e-11 at step 40, order 1 by step 140); max/rate bounds them.
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 4 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
velocity        all create 1.44 87287 loop geom
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0
timestep        0.005
fix             1 all nve
fix             2 all deform/pressure 1 x trate 0.1 y volume z volume vol/balance/p yes max/rate 0.2
compute         tdef all temp/deform
thermo_style    custom step temp c_tdef press pxx pyy pzz lx ly lz vol
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          20
run             160
